# Copy to .env.
#
# EVERYTHING HERE IS PUBLIC. Anything prefixed EXPO_PUBLIC_ is compiled into the
# app bundle in plain text and readable by anyone who unpacks the APK. Expo says
# this explicitly, and it is why no session token, API key or secret of any kind
# may appear in this file -- not even a development one, because a development
# shortcut that works is a shortcut that ships.
#
# Credentials belong in device secure storage, obtained by signing in.

# Where the account service lives. Caddy mounts it under /auth and strips the
# prefix, so the app appends /devices and /health to this.
EXPO_PUBLIC_ACCOUNT_URL=https://staging.consummate7.com/auth

# Developer switch: 1 shows the call diagnostics line (voice legs, ICE, transport
# events) on the call screen. Off in every build a person installs.
EXPO_PUBLIC_CALL_DIAGNOSTICS=

# --- Google sign-in ---
# OAuth client ids from Google Cloud project `consummate-7`, created 3 Oct 2026.
# These belong in this file precisely BECAUSE everything here is public: a
# Google client id is an identifier, not a credential, and the Android and iOS
# clients have no secret at all. What protects them is the signing certificate
# (Android) and the bundle id (iOS) registered alongside each one, which is why
# an APK signed with any other key cannot use them.
#
# The app asks Google for an ID TOKEN and sends only that to the account
# service; it never sees, stores or forwards a Google access token. The web
# client id is sent as the audience so the token the server receives is one the
# server can verify against its own list.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=692573915541-13t0122j4bd8vkgkainvh91cjt9vfdil.apps.googleusercontent.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID=692573915541-sbq8ila7tjkptd9ueqfdan9n6gm5tb81.apps.googleusercontent.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=692573915541-05d8gnhk6b9s7mvkqk4vg169cr3qe39n.apps.googleusercontent.com
